/* Dead-server recovery.  RECOVERY_INTERVAL_CS is the shortest wait between probes, keeping TryRecoverServer below the
 * callevery cadence.  RECOVERY_MAX_INTERVAL_CS is the longest wait failed probes back off to: each probe can stall the desktop
 * for its connect budget, RECOVERY_PROBE_CS, so a dead mount nobody is using is probed rarely, and using it brings the probe
 * back to RECOVERY_INTERVAL_CS.  After RECOVERY_PROBE_LIMIT probes the cached address is given up, so the next call
 * reconnects from scratch.
 */
